{"body":"## Summary\n\nAdd the smallest explicit test-only expected-Postgres-port seam needed to run #944 against fresh disposable resources. The existing diagnostic fixture validates worker URLs against the historical hard-coded port `61169`; #944 correctly forbids reusing that old tuple and reserves fresh ports. Without a seam, the exact F16/F17 evidence recovery stops before behavior.\n\nThis issue changes only test harness validation. It does not change production behavior, database schemas, runtime guards, selectors, or assertions.\n\n## Governing references\n\n- Parent campaign: #897\n- Blocked evidence recovery: #944\n- Source candidate: `5b60645bae20e416781cda66b98123635f209341` / tree `5621d4bb2bbd47967132812d68ae5beb9f7172f6`\n- Failure evidence: #944 first attempt, fixture dependency `owned_worker_database`; the unchanged fixture requires port `61169`.\n- Existing worker URL setup: `apps/api/test/helpers/testDatabases.ts`, `apps/api/test/globalSetup.ts`, `apps/api/test/setup-env.ts`.\n\n## Owner and delivery\n\n- GitHub assignee: `bagtyyarkovusov`\n- One isolated implementer from the exact base above; coordinator is sole issue-update owner and assembler.\n- Required model: `codex_work/gpt-6.1-sol`, service `default`, `xhigh` for implementation/review, full access.\n- After assembly, exact-SHA Standards and Spec reviews are required before #944 reruns.\n\n## Allowed paths\n\n- `apps/api/test/helpers/diagnosticPreparedReaderFixture.ts`\n- One new direct boundary test beside the helper under `apps/api/test/helpers/**` proving the seam's default and explicit behavior\n- Evidence only under `docs/evidence/issue-897/a-06-combined-ci-20261030/prepared-source-boundary-20261103/full-coverage-20261103/issue945-port-seam-20261104/**`\n\nNo other source, production, config, dependency, migration, workflow, selector, or package files may change.\n\n## Required behavior\n\n- Introduce one explicit environment seam, for example `DIAGNOSTIC_EXPECTED_POSTGRES_PORT`, used only by the fixture's ownership validation.\n- The default remains the historical `61169` so existing callers retain their current contract.\n- When the environment value is provided, validate a strict decimal TCP port and use it for the expected worker database URL; reject absent, malformed, non-integer, or out-of-range values through the existing fixture dependency path.\n- Do not derive the port from an arbitrary URL, silently fall back when the override is malformed, or weaken hostname/database-name/Redis/MinIO ownership checks.\n- Preserve `VITEST_POOL_ID=1` as an explicit runtime prerequisite in #944; this issue does not alter worker allocation.\n- Add a focused boundary test for default, valid override, and invalid override behavior without starting services.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run the focused helper boundary test, API typecheck, verified TS6, lint, build, and `git diff --check` serially.\n- Capture exact source/evidence SHAs, raw command outputs and hashes, and the allow-list diff.\n- Prove no production path or migration changed.\n- Fresh exact-SHA Standards/Spec reviews must pass.\n- #944 must then repin to the resulting source SHA before any runtime reservation.\n\n## Out of scope and stop rules\n\n- No F16/F17 runtime in this issue, no services/resources, no broad test suite, no reporter changes, no source assertion changes, no PR #904 mutation.\n- Stop if the seam would need production code, a new package/config dependency, a selector change, or broader fixture refactoring.\n\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOScB2L88AAAABil4rZA","author":{"login":"bagtyyarkovusov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Parent created this bounded test-only seam from source base 5b60645bae20e416781cda66b98123635f209341 after #944 stopped on the historical hard-coded PG61169 dependency. The existing A coordinator owns dispatch, assembly and issue updates; #944 remains held until this seam is assembled and reviewed.","createdAt":"2026-11-03T21:55:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Carberk/carberk/issues/945#issuecomment-6616394596","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOScB2L88AAAABil7epA","author":{"login":"bagtyyarkovusov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## #945 bounded writer dispatched\n\nThe current coordinator was revalidated clean at `39c63fad462885846840149b15771654980bdaa7` / tree `ea4f2d4b3b397a0e6cfd1e72064b5e0421b4e35d`; its non-documentation source remains byte-equal to the requested #945 base `5b60645bae20e416781cda66b98123635f209341` / tree `5621d4bb`. #944 cleanup/terminal evidence is preserved; no #944 rerun is authorized.\n\nOne isolated implementer only was dispatched:\n<t3-thread://v2/ce9be202-17c9-4f76-8357-807251606a41/thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A02fb8109-0de1-4383-a1f0-8999ce3de3ac%3Adelegate-task%3Aissue945-port-seam-run52>\n\nSettings read back: `codex_work/gpt-6.1-sol`, `xhigh`, serviceTier `default`, full-access. Scope is limited to the fixture, one focused helper boundary test and #945 evidence. No #944 runtime, resources, production/config/dependency/selector/assertion changes, #942/F43 work or PR904 action. The writer must preserve #944's `VITEST_POOL_ID=1` prerequisite.","createdAt":"2026-11-03T21:58:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Carberk/carberk/issues/945#issuecomment-6616440484","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOScB2L88AAAABimK6xw","author":{"login":"bagtyyarkovusov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## #945 writer wait verified\n\nThe live contract is unchanged. The sole isolated writer is still undelivered: no terminal handoff or terminal evidence receipt is available. Its worktree remains at committed red checkpoint `785aaef5d` on `t3/issue-945-diagnostic-postgres-port-seam`, with `apps/api/test/helpers/diagnosticPreparedReaderFixture.ts` still modified in the worktree. I did not inspect, edit, assemble, or replace that work.\n\nCoordinator remains clean and unchanged at `39c63fad462885846840149b15771654980bdaa7` / tree `ea4f2d4b3b397a0e6cfd1e72064b5e0421b4e35d`; its non-documentation source remains the reviewed #939 candidate. No #945 source/evidence audit, assembly, fresh review, #944 rerun, #942/F43/prototype work, PR904 action, or runtime reservation is authorized until the existing writer delivers its terminal handoff.\n\nExisting writer link: <t3-thread://v2/ce9be202-17c9-4f76-8357-807251606a41/thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A02fb8109-0de1-4383-a1f0-8999ce3de3ac%3Adelegate-task%3Aissue945-port-seam-run52>","createdAt":"2026-11-03T22:11:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Carberk/carberk/issues/945#issuecomment-6616693447","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":945,"state":"OPEN","title":"[A test seam] Parameterize diagnostic fixture expected Postgres port","updatedAt":"2026-11-03T22:12:00Z","url":"https://github.com/Carberk/carberk/issues/945"}
